              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The majority held that \u00a7\u202f1028A(a)(1) requires the means of identification to be at the crux of the criminal conduct, thereby imposing a mandatory two\u2011year minimum sentence."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dd608b26387f3e95842727f879e7c8ae6197059dca88b53e669a28622230f8c9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dd608b26387f-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "dd608b26387f3e95842727f879e7c8ae6197059dca88b53e669a28622230f8c9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dd608b26387f-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 27
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "dd608b26387f3e95842727f879e7c8ae6197059dca88b53e669a28622230f8c9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dd608b26387f-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 31,
              "start": 31
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Gorsuch filed a concurrence warning that the Court\u2019s interpretation could label many ordinary adults as aggravated identity thieves and emphasizing that a causal relationship is required for liability."
      }
    ],
